# A double click selects the word at the pointer: the run of cells up to a
# space, punctuation included, at the start, the middle and the end of a
# row. On a space it selects nothing, so the copy that follows copies
# nothing. On the empty cells after a row's text it selects nothing too, so
# the last copy copies nothing and the frame shows no selected cell.
# spec: ADR-1003, the selection; INTERFACE-vtium.md, The selection and copy
# covers: clipboard.selection
size 20 2
send "one two,three  four\r\nab"
select word at 0,0
copy
select word at 5,0
copy
select word at 18,0
copy
select word at 13,0
copy
select word at 5,1
copy
dump frame
